session:pr804Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #711 asked whether the W3C OWL 2 Mapping to RDF Graphs spec defines an encoding for meta-annotations (annotations on an annotation), since owl_to_rdf.rs only reified axiom-level annotations via owl:Axiom and left nested Annotation.annotations unreified in both directions. Rather than trust issue #589's claim about an owl:Annotation-typed blank node encoding, the live spec text (Translation of Annotations, Table 2, S2.2) was fetched and read directly: TANN is genuinely recursive, using owl:Annotation (not owl:Axiom) for the nested reification, with the same annotatedSource/annotatedProperty/annotatedTarget shape, confirming #589's claim. Implemented both directions: Translator::emit_annotation (OWL->RDF) as the recursive TANN(ann, y) helper, generalizing the existing per-annotation loop in emit_axiom_annotations so the same code path handles both the top-level owl:Axiom case and nested owl:Annotation cases; and class_expression_parser::meta_annotations (RDF->OWL) as its mirror, searching for an owl:Annotation reification node matching a given (subject, property, value) triple and recursing. Added a round-trip integration test using owl_functional_parser (whose grammar already supports nested Annotation(Annotation(...) ...) syntax from #695/#709) feeding through owl2rdf and back through rdf2owl." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:804 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr804 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr804Decision .

session:pr804Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "Discovered mid-task that issue #589 ('Annotation has no representation for nested annotations-on-annotations') asks for exactly the RDF-encoding half of what #711 scopes, and is also at Status Agent. Decided not to pick up #589 in this session (CLAUDE.md forbids starting a second issue's work mid-task without review) and instead to flag it explicitly in the PR body and plan doc as superseded/duplicate once #711 merges, since #589's structural premise (no Vec<Annotation> field to populate) went stale once #695/#709 landed before #589's remaining RDF-encoding ask was ever implemented." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered just closing #589 directly as duplicate once the overlap was found; rejected per CLAUDE.md's rule that only the user (Dag), not an agent, closes/supersedes another issue — left as an explicit recommendation in the PR body for Dag's review instead." .
